Hey and thanks, I’ll cover the topic of sensitive PII first:

It is prohibited by OpenAI, we currently send ticket contents (what a user has written to us) to their platform for processing. Technically it’s impossible to guarantee that data does *not* include sensitive PII - for example a user could disclose their religion or sexual orientation to us in a ticket…

We strive to avoid such situations, but you should be aware it will always be impossible to 100% prevent, given the highly fuzzy nature of sensitive PII.

Regarding other questions:

{quote}* Would it be only data we have in Beehive when the user makes a request or would it be all data we store about the user in Admin?{quote}

The purpose of the trial is to assess many different use cases at Bolt - customer support, marketing, data analytics, even Legal if you folks are interested 🙂 When it comes to user data, most use-cases are generally *not* going to include PII, but rather business data (aggregated and non-aggregated). The most extreme situation of processing customer data would be the example we already do - sending ticket contents.

{quote}* Would you fuel the Chat with the safety incident data?{quote}

This is not anticipated, but I’ll discuss more with any Safety team folk before we would include them in the trial.

{quote}* What would you do with this data using the Chat? What type of work would this include?{quote}

It’s hard to say in general - every use-case and team would have different points of value. For example Marketing may want to generate some copy for email campaigns. CS team may want to analyse some CS tickets in bulk to get deeper insights. Analysts may want to feed it some csv or business data (orders with prices, distances etc) to run some exploratory analysis.

{quote}* As you said, you want to freely test it, is there a specific result that would suggest the trial is successful?{quote}

Generally speaking we’re looking to validate that it will speed up how internal teams work, while not reducing quality of their output, or even increasing quality of output in some cases.

{quote}* Selected group of people at Bolt: who would be that people?{quote}

Hard to say right now, depends on the use-cases, but it can be heavily controlled based on your feedback as needed 🙂 

{quote}* Would you use the data of only active users or deleted as well?{quote}

If any PII is needed to be processed we can keep it restricted to active users. Non PII from deleted users may be needed, eg. count of some orders in the past, some of which are from users no longer on the platform.

{quote}* How many markets and users would be affected?{quote}

We should consider all markets and potentially all recently active users (last 12 months eg)

{quote}* Is there any negative impact on users during the trial like suspension, blocking, risk of not providing good quality CS services?{quote}

No risks at all. Generally this should help internal employees to do their job faster at same or better quality.

{quote}* Do we need to sign any agreement for the trial? You mentioned the use is covered by the initial agreement, does it include the trial? Can you please share the initial agreement signed?{quote}

No signed agreement needed for the trial. I don’t have access to/copy of our API platform agreement, but I presume it exists in our Legal systems/database?

