Hey, [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d]!


You are right, the primary obligation to verify age is imposed on Auchan by the regulation that enables them to have a licence to sell age restricted goods. However, in our T&Cs for couriers we ask couriers to verify the age. Auchan wants to exclude their liability in case courier fails to verify the age. We can add this wording to the agreement with Auchan in which case their contractual liability will be excluded, but Auchan still will be one responsible due to obligations arising outside of the contract. Couriers have mainly contractual obligations to verify age (perhaps there are some local regulations in this regard, but since they have no licence their responsibilities are different than Auchan’s).

I am not sure that couriers will be acting on behalf of Auchan, because there is no contractual relationship between Courier and Auchan. Contractual relationship wise there is a contractual relationships between:

# Courier and Client (Delivery Agreement);
# Courier and Bolt (T&Cs);
# Partner and Client (Sales Agreement);
# Partner and Bolt (T&Cs);
# Bolt and Client (T&Cs).

Therefore, I understand that age verification as a data processing should be covered in the Delivery Agreement concluded between Client and Courier or in the T&Cs between Bolt and Client in which case Courier verifies age on behalf of Bolt, because Bolt imposes this contractual obligation on the Courier.

I attach a picture of contractual relationships just in case. Please review and let me know what do you think.



