* In general, the less data of riders/drivers we have and use, the less privacy problems there are. To have less problems from privacy perspective (i.e. to minimize the amount of personal data we collect), it would be best to make sure we leave as less space for the users to share the photos of their face.
** For this reason, I was wondering (and I saw some comments in the Confluence page, but it’s still unclear to me) - do we absolutely need to enable the users to take photos of their front camera? I see no value in enabling this for the drivers; for riders - it’s hard to imagine a scenario when a rider would be taking a photo without his face with a front camera.

{color:#0747a6}The reasoning behind the front-facing camera is due to the fact that riders will be looking at the road/parking lot when waiting. The rear camera will be pointing at the other side of the street. The assumption is that when taking a photo, the rider might take the easiest path and snap a photo of what is in front of them, which is the other side of the road, leading the driver to the wrong side of the road. This is, however, an assumption and not a fact.{color}



* Are we going to test this feature? If so, in what markets?

{color:#0747a6}Yes. The exact countries are not yet defined, however, the goal will be to launch globally. Are there preferred countries for testing, in terms of privacy concerns?{color}



* What is the reason to store it for 30 days?
** Is this period tied to any other retention periods (e.g. refunds, claims)?
*** {color:#0747a6}Not really. It’s the default storing retention for chats too, thus we were using the same period.{color}
** How long does it usually take us to take action regarding a wrong pick-up location?
*** {color:#0747a6}We normally don’t take actions on these cases{color}
** What would we (CS/other teams) use the pictures for?
*** {color:#0747a6}CS has access to chats up to 30d old. Stored pictures would be used mainly for analysing harassment or misuse of the feature.{color}
** Why would a rider/driver need to see 30 days old photos?
*** {color:#0747a6}They won’t. Riders and Drivers can see photos only while they have access to the chat. The chat is automatically unavailable to them, as soon as the order is finished or cancelled.{color}
* Would it be possible to add a disclaimer somewhere (perhaps [*here*|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4837113935/20240226+Pick-up+Photo+Sharing+in+Chat#:~:text=20240319%2D082914.png-,User%20guidance,-In%20order%20to]) in the app that the photos will be shared other party and Bolt and stored for X period for Y reasons?
** {color:#0747a6}There is already a disclaimer on the top of each chat stating “Please note Bolt can access your conversations with the driver.” (and vice versa) and a link to the Privacy Policy. Do you believe it’s necessary to tell the user that the photo added to the chat will be shared with the other party? Sounds a little redundant, based on what the feature is about, a chat.{color}
!Screenshot 2024-05-02 at 15.27.43.png|width=508,height=659,alt="Screenshot 2024-05-02 at 15.27.43.png"!
* During what time will it be possible to send the photo? Will the option be disabled once the pickup is confirmed? Will it be possible to send a photo after the trip is finished if a chat between Rider<>Driver was initiated before?
** {color:#0747a6}We are allowing for availability during the entirety of the order. We’re not disabling after pick-up as an order can have multiple stops. Users engage with the chat, when returning to the vehicle on one of the stops. A photo can be used then, for the same reasoning.{color}
** {color:#0747a6}It will not be possible to send a photo after the trip is finished as the chat will not be available to any of the parties.{color}
* If the driver/rider accidentally took a photo of something that they didn’t want to and send it - what would be the process of deleting this picture from the chat/our systems?
** {color:#0747a6}Currently, there is no deleting process, same as for chat messages. The user will have access to a “Confirmation Screen” before sending the photo. On confirming it, they are accepting this photo will be sent to the driver and the policies ruling the chat {color}[{color:#0747a6}(Figma design link){color}|https://www.figma.com/file/F795UftE6AzxAF6xDOc8nd/Rider-Chat?type=design&node-id=8165-32711&mode=design&t=F7U6GZAWIvLGTpnh-0]{color:#0747a6} {color}
